#errorCatcher Echo
##############################################################################
## strings.json.tmpl -- the client-side translation dictionary.
##
## Generates jsondata/strings.json: EVERY language's full phrase set in one
## payload, nested by language code:
##
##   {"da": {"Temperature": "Temperatur", "Min": "Min", ...},
##    "fr": {"Temperature": "Température", ...},
##    ...}
##
## Built entirely on the Python side ($divumwx_strings_payload, see
## bin/user/divumwx_cards.py's DivumwxCards._read_all_lang_strings) by
## reading every skins/DivumWX/lang/*.conf file directly with configobj --
## deliberately NOT via $gettext(), which only ever has access to the ONE
## lang file matching this report's own configured `lang` setting. That
## single-language limitation is exactly why this file used to contain
## ~260 individual $gettext(...) calls (one render = one language baked
## in); reading every file directly sidesteps it entirely, and lets the
## client switch languages in the browser -- the same way its existing
## unit-system dropdown switches km/h to mph -- without a server round
## trip, since every language's text is already sitting in this one file.
##
## KEEPING THIS FILE IN SYNC WITH en.conf:
## This template no longer lists individual phrases -- there's nothing
## here to keep in sync with en.conf any more. Adding a phrase to a card
## now means: add the key to en.conf (and any language you're translating
## it into) with a real value; skins/DivumWX/lang/*.conf's own [Texts]
## keys ARE the source of truth this file reads from directly. A key
## missing from a given language's .conf simply isn't in that language's
## sub-object below -- DivumWXI18N.t() (cardI18n.js) falls back to the key
## itself (English) for that one phrase, same one-string-at-a-time
## fallback behaviour as always, so a partial translation never breaks
## the page.
##
## A single malformed lang/*.conf file is skipped (with a logged warning),
## not fatal to this render -- see _read_all_lang_strings()'s own comment
## for why: archive.json/charts.json share this same search list
## extension instance, so one bad translation file must not take the
## whole report down.
##
## The whole payload (including the "_default" language marker) is built
## entirely in Python (see $divumwx_strings_payload's own comment in
## divumwx_cards.py) and handed here as one already-valid-JSON string --
## this template does no JSON construction of its own, on purpose.
##############################################################################
$divumwx_strings_payload
